From: WinBoat
Subject: [PATCH] vkr: VK_EXT_device_generated_commands

The host drivers have it (NVIDIA 570 on), the Venus protocol didn't: vkd3d-proton takes it for ExecuteIndirect
tier 1.1 (incrementing constants) and for every ExecuteIndirect that changes state per command (without it those
record nothing). The protocol headers are venus-protocol's
generator output (git-9fa07f3c plus the video branch) with VK_KHR_maintenance8 and VK_EXT_device_generated_commands
in its extension list; the extension's commands are numbered 1100-1108 (clear of upstream's numbering, as the video
commands' 1000-1015). Maintenance8's generated code is the hand-written one of 0011, plus its
VkMemoryBarrierAccessFlags3KHR in subpass dependencies. vkr: indirect commands layouts (objects), the memory
requirements query, preprocess/execute. Indirect execution sets aren't dispatched (the guest driver offers no stage
for them). The generator learned unions whose tags select no member (the token data of dispatch and draw
tokens): the tag alone goes on the wire and the renderer zeroes the union; other unknown tags stay fatal.
---
